  "solution": {
    "text": "Sulphur of organic compounds is detected by using sodium nitroprusside. With it sulphur forms a violet colour complex, called sodium thionitroprusside.<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>NO</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>Sodium</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nitroprusside</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>NOS</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>Violet</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>colour</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
